       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. That's true even with normal kidney and liver function. A dose that high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. The shock can be refractory and can come with non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nPlease check whether one of these was intended:\n- **5 mg once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg once daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **Another drug or dose**, if a different medication was meant.\n\nIf 50 mg is deliberate, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that. For example, you might be using it as part of a specific protocol. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
